CHANGES
=======

Version 0.99.35 (2026-09-07)
----------------------------
* Recognize standing user authorization for project memory updates.
* Simplify command dispatch, instruction rendering and skill handling without
  changing their behavior.

Version 0.99.34 (2026-09-07)
----------------------------
* Keep the agent-brain socket under the configured root so the service and
  MCP clients connect regardless of their environment. Restart the service
  and agent sessions after upgrading.
* Remove the runtime-directory environment variable from the service helper.

Version 0.99.33 (2026-09-06)
----------------------------
* Run the agent-brain MCP server as `agent-brain` from `PATH` and choose its
  socket when the bridge starts, so generated agent configuration no longer
  contains the path of whichever install rendered it. Re-render existing
  profiles with `agent-run update`.
* Let the git guard through for throwaway test repositories: `commit`, `tag`
  and `push` run normally below a directory holding an `.agent-run-test-repo`
  marker, so a project's own test suite works inside an agent session.
* Match the git guard on the subcommand instead of any argument, so
  `git log --grep push` or a branch named `commit` is no longer blocked.
* Fix the Windows guard shims: strip a leading PATH entry only when it is the
  guard directory, resolve the real command explicitly, and refuse recursive
  resolution.
* Archive closed review findings to a compact history file and add
  `review_history` for recalling them without them appearing in normal
  knowledge retrieval.
* Keep brain retrieval working when a single knowledge or task file is
  malformed, reporting the broken file instead of failing every read.
* Rebuild the search index only when the underlying files change, so read-only
  retrieval no longer writes on every call.
* Run brain Git operations against the real git binary rather than the guard
  shim, and stage `templates/` with `sync save`.
* Render skills through a loader restricted to the skills directories, so a
  skill template cannot include files elsewhere in the configuration root.
* Omit disabled MCP servers from Codex and Grok configuration, as Claude and
  Gemini already do.
* Remove `AGENT_WRAPPER_FORCE_PERMISSIVE`, the undocumented environment
  variable that disabled Claude's permission prompts.
* Stop overwriting systemd units and helper scripts in the configuration root
  on every run.
* Remove `scripts/release-check.sh`. `pnpm release` now only creates and pushes
  the tag, and `pnpm run release:preflight` is a clean build plus the tests.

Version 0.99.32 (2026-09-06)
----------------------------
* Add severity, an assigned C1/H1/M1/L1 label, and an open/fixed/wontfix state
  to review knowledge, with `review_list` and `resolve_review` for working
  through findings in priority order.
* Add `amend_knowledge` to revise an active item in place, keeping its id, file
  name, and history.
* Let `remember` choose a file name instead of the item id, with the id appended
  when that name is taken.
* Read the package version from `package.json` in one place instead of a second
  copy in the source, so the version agent-brain reports cannot drift.
* Fix task updates resetting every field the caller did not mention, which made
  completing a task discard its description, priority, labels, and notes.

Version 0.99.31 (2026-09-06)
----------------------------
* Add agent-brain for shared project knowledge, skills, review context and
  tasks through a per-user MCP service on a private Unix socket.
* Add project creation and registration, global/project/default scopes,
  Markdown knowledge with SQLite search, and structured task storage.
* Add read-only GitHub and Trello task imports and explicit Git synchronization
  for portable knowledge, with revision checks and conflict reporting.
* Connect all four native agents to the brain and preserve existing profiles,
  memory and skill templates.
* Create the standard knowledge directories and explain automatic placement
  by scope and type in the brain-memory skill.
* Add optional systemd service management for selected users, including safe
  startup pulls, and consolidate project documentation in README.md.

Version 0.99.30 (2026-09-06)
----------------------------
* Add native Gemini CLI and Grok Build adapters alongside Codex and Claude
  Code, with private runtimes, shared instructions, skills, and MCP servers.
* Add `agent-run gemini`, `agent-run grok`, and a native capability matrix
  through `agent-run status`.
* Keep vendor configuration and launch options behind a common adapter
  interface, with native arguments passed through to the selected CLI.
* Add Gemini and Grok to the AI tools updater, use fixed `/usr/local` paths,
  install pnpm last, and remove recurring command-shim deletion.
* Update the starter configuration, documentation, and integration tests for
  all four native agents.

Version 0.99.29 (2026-09-04)
----------------------------
* Add tracked per-profile project memory under `notes/memory`, while keeping
  native Codex memories in ignored machine-local runtime state.
* Detect older memory layouts before profile updates and agent launches, ask
  before staging tracked moves with `git mv`, and support
  `migrate-config --yes` for non-interactive migrations.
* Make copied systemd updater files portable, install the helper under
  `/usr/local/libexec`, and remove stale AI tool launchers before global
  package updates.
* Explain the shared configuration model for native coding agents in the
  README.

Version 0.99.28 (2026-08-30)
----------------------------
* Add interactive `agent-run setup [org/repo]`, make `agent-run generate` the
  profile-initialization command, and retain `init` as a deprecated alias.
* Use `~/.agent-run` as the single default config directory, overridable with
  `--configdir`, `AGENT_CONFIG_DIR`, or a project-local `.agent-run.env`.
* Resolve profiles from `package.json.repository` and avoid rewriting unchanged
  generated files.

Version 0.99.27 (2026-08-11)
----------------------------
* Rename the unattended-run option from `--danger` to `--yolo` for Codex and
  Claude.
* Add `agent-run setup [config-root]` to create the packaged starter agent
  configuration files without overwriting local edits.
* Resolve plain directories without Git metadata or a package name as
  `[parent]/[current]` profiles.

Version 0.99.26 (2026-07-31)
----------------------------
* Add `--danger` support for Claude so unattended runs pass
  `--dangerously-skip-permissions`.
* Remove Claude's generated `.claude/settings.local.json` after guarded runs,
  while preserving project-local settings when `--local` is used.
* Keep nested command-guard tests independent of an outer agent-run session's
  executable search path.

Version 0.99.25 (2026-07-11)
----------------------------
* Add config-root `agent-run.defaults.jsonc` inheritance so project manifests
  contain only overrides, with nested-object merging and array replacement.
* Stop creating empty local templates and override directories, require an
  explicit sparse profile marker for updates and tool runs, and keep `edit` as
  the command that creates local instructions.
* Split the TypeScript CLI into focused parsing, configuration, rendering,
  project-discovery, checking, process, and tool-runtime modules.

Version 0.99.24 (2026-07-11)
----------------------------
* Allow failed tag releases to be retried through a manual workflow dispatch,
  and omit npm provenance when the GitHub source repository is private.
* Reinstall pnpm after Corepack updates so `/usr/local/bin/pnpm` runs the latest
  npm-installed pnpm while projects keep honoring their pinned package manager.

Version 0.99.23 (2026-07-11)
----------------------------
* Load Codex instructions, configuration, and skills natively from the private
  `CODEX_HOME`, and default to `on-request` with the `workspace-write` sandbox.
* Load Claude instructions through `--append-system-prompt-file`, load generated
  skills as a strictly valid local plugin, and preserve the user's normal Claude
  configuration.
* Prevent shell injection in editor and child-process launches, fix generated
  command guards, honor guardrail flags, and remove stale generated skills.
* Fix literal argument forwarding, workspace and worktree resolution, deep and
  ignored repository discovery, current local-agent detection, and fenced legacy
  imports.
* Enforce per-profile tool and local-agent-file switches, and preserve clean
  executable lookup paths across nested agent-run sessions.
* Escape generated JSON and TOML paths portably, validate Claude settings, and
  protect or migrate legacy Codex credentials and runtime state.
* Make releases reproducible by pinning GitHub Actions, using frozen installs,
  and publishing the exact packed artifact with npm provenance.
* Keep the global npm updater under `/usr/local`, avoid modifying distro-owned
  paths or host-wide configuration, and install Claude's native binary when npm
  blocks package lifecycle scripts.

Version 0.99.22 (2026-06-27)
----------------------------
* Default generated Codex configs to `danger-full-access` while keeping `--sandboxed` as an explicit opt-in.
* Search common global config-root locations on Windows and Unix, including both `agent-config` and `agent-configs`.
* Fix release script package metadata reads under Git Bash on Windows.
* Document the config-root discovery order and add regression coverage for the generated sandbox mode and search candidates.

Version 0.99.21 (2026-06-27)
----------------------------
* Default project commands for `[code]/owner/repo` checkouts to `[code]/agent-config`.
* Make `update --all` map profiles under a colocated `agent-config` root back to their matching project roots.
* Expand integration coverage for the colocated config-root layout and Windows command/path behavior.

Version 0.99.20 (2026-06-03)
----------------------------
* Add systemd unit templates and install tooling for the global AI tools updater.
* Add a login warning helper that prints a large banner when `~/.agent-config` has uncommitted changes.

Version 0.99.19 (2026-06-03)
----------------------------
* Link per-profile Codex `auth.json` files to the shared `~/.codex/auth.json` login cache when available.
* Add `agent-run update --all [config-root]` to regenerate every profile from the config tree without requiring code checkouts.

Version 0.99.18 (2026-05-26)
----------------------------
* Remove extensionless Node command shim lookup on Windows so generated guard shims resolve real executables correctly.
* Generate Windows guard shims with LF endings so generated-file checks stay stable with repository line-ending rules.

Version 0.99.17 (2026-05-06)
----------------------------
* Generate Codex native skills under `CODEX_HOME/skills` so runtime skill discovery matches generated profiles.
* Remove stale legacy Codex skill copies from `live/.agents/skills` during profile updates.

Version 0.99.16 (2026-05-03)
----------------------------
* Move review history out of generated `live/` directories into persistent profile `reviews/` directories and migrate legacy live review files.
* Rename the built-in review skill to `code-review-organizer` and remove stale generated `code-review` skill directories.
* Add the `release-package-check` skill to replace the external `repo-check` package release checklist.

Version 0.99.15 (2026-04-30)
----------------------------
* Add `--generate` for Codex and Claude runs to render generated files without launching the underlying tool.

Version 0.99.14 (2026-04-30)
----------------------------
* Add `--show` for Codex and Claude runs to print the tool-specific source templates/includes and generated files without launching the underlying tool.

Version 0.99.13 (2026-04-27)
----------------------------
* Render each profile's generated files and runtime state under `live/`, leaving the profile root for source config and templates.

Version 0.99.12 (2026-04-27)
----------------------------
* Add `--local` for Codex and Claude runs to warn about local AI files instead of failing.
* Limit generated Claude permission allow entries to configured checks instead of broad blocked command families.
* Write agent-run's Claude settings to `.claude/agent-run-settings.json` and remove only exact legacy generated `.claude/settings.json` files.

Version 0.99.11 (2026-04-27)
----------------------------
* Show the package version in `agent-run --help` and add `agent-run --version`.

Version 0.99.10 (2026-04-27)
----------------------------
* Add `paths.globalMemoryDir` to render context and expose it from default Codex, Claude, AGENTS, and CLAUDE templates.

Version 0.99.9 (2026-04-26)
---------------------------
* Add `{config-root}/notes/memory` as an optional shared memory directory passed with `--add-dir` to Codex and Claude when it exists.
* Add a starter `skills/personal-memory.md` file to the packaged config skeleton.

Version 0.99.8 (2026-04-26)
---------------------------
* Skip stale `codex` or `claude` PATH redirect shims that print `Run agent-run instead` when locating the real underlying tool binary.

Version 0.99.7 (2026-04-26)
---------------------------
* Add a checked-in basic starter config under `examples/basic-config` that exercises manifests, templates, snippets, skills, overrides, guardrails, checks, and generated runtime paths.
* Add `agent-run --init [config-root]` to copy the packaged starter config skeleton to a destination, defaulting to `~/.agent-config`.
* Replace the placeholder test command with an integration test suite covering the starter config, rendering, checking, stale-file detection, guard shims, local AI-file detection, and flexible command parsing.

Version 0.99.6 (2026-04-26)
---------------------------
* Allow `agent-run` to find the target command after wrapper arguments, so invocations like `agent-run --sandboxed --network codex` work the same as `agent-run codex --sandboxed --network`.

Version 0.99.5 (2026-04-25)
---------------------------
* Bootstrap missing default global templates, manifests, local templates, and overrides before `agent-run codex`, `agent-run claude`, or `agent-run update` render a profile.
* Avoid rewriting the config-root `.gitignore` when it already contains the generated-file ignore entries.

Version 0.99.4 (2026-04-24)
---------------------------
* Refactor profile generation around `agent-run.jsonc` manifests, Nunjucks templates, generated Codex and Claude homes, and private per-profile runtime output.
* Add generated native skill files, Codex `config.toml`, Claude `settings.json`, guard command shims, and a config-root `.gitignore` for generated outputs.
* Add Codex runtime modes with `--danger`, `--sandboxed`, and `--network`, defaulting to a private `CODEX_HOME` plus explicit `-C` project root handling.
* Change the default config root to `~/.agent-config`, add `AGENT_CONFIG_DIR`, and preserve existing config-root overrides.
* Add `agent-run migrate-config` for converting legacy `AGENTS-MODS.md` config trees into the new manifest/template layout.
* Add `jsonc-parser` and `nunjucks` runtime dependencies for JSONC manifests and template rendering.
* Add `-h` and `--help` output for `agent-run` and its built-in commands, while keeping `agent-run codex --help` and `agent-run claude --help` as passthrough to the underlying tools.
* Make `agent-run check` compare `AGENTS.md` against the same expanded template output that `agent-run update` writes, so placeholder-based profiles no longer fail as stale immediately after update.

Version 0.99.3 (2026-04-08)
---------------------------
* Replace the GitHub release action with `gh` so the workflow avoids the remaining Node 20 action warning.

Version 0.99.2 (2026-04-08)
---------------------------
* Update the release workflow to use current GitHub Actions versions that run on Node 24.
* Skip npm publish in the release workflow when the package version already exists on npm.

Version 0.99.1 (2026-04-08)
---------------------------
* Expand `{{AGENT_DIR}}`, `{{AGENTS_PATH}}`, and related placeholders from `AGENTS-MODS.md` when generating `AGENTS.md`.
* Make `pnpm release` create and push the release tag so GitHub Actions owns npm publishing.

Version 0.99.0 (2026-03-19)
---------------------------
* Normalize package metadata and license copyright text to `Technomoron.com`.

Version 0.99.0 (2026-03-19)
---------------------------
* Replace the shell wrapper with the Node and TypeScript-based `agent-run` utility.
* Add `check` and `init` commands, source-root support, and external agent-config mapping.
* Add `.agent-run-ignore` and `.agent-run.env` support for explicit ignore and profile overrides.
* Add a full README describing the tool, workflow, and mapping model.
* Add `edit` support for opening mapped `AGENTS-MODS.md`, including VS Code terminal handling and editor fallbacks.
* Move bundled project agent configs out of this repo into the external `agent-configs` tree.
